{
  "version": 1,
  "$comment": "Former Smart bundle names the Loader still answers to. A forward is not a rule in the distribution (a rule of type smart is a Smart component to the registry, and a forward has no element); the Loader installs it at start as a rule with no tags, no assets and one relation, the new name, unless a rule of that name is already defined, and a relation that names a forward is taken as its target, so the element waits for the bundle itself. Each forward is dated and has a change journal record; remove it on remove_after. A forward may lead to a component package's rule (cl-table -> cl-view-table, package pro, rename plan R2): the Loader follows it once the package's rules are registered, and a package that still registers the former name itself (one built before the rename) keeps its own rule, which the forward then leaves alone.",
